# Nivaran environment settings
# 1. Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env
# 2. Paste your real keys into .env (NOT into this file)
# 3. .env is in .gitignore, so it is never uploaded to GitHub
# On Vercel, add the same names under Project > Settings > Environment Variables.

# ---------- AI provider (required: fill in ONE) ----------

# Google Gemini (default). Use a key with billing enabled:
# free-tier keys hit rate limits after ~25-30 calls a minute.
# Get it at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI (alternative). Get it at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------- Supabase (optional, recommended) ----------
# Stores the SOP knowledge base and a numbers-only log of every AI request.
# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API.
# Use the SERVICE ROLE / secret key, NOT the anon key. It stays on the server.
# Leave both empty to use data/sops.json and skip logging.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=

# ---------- Optional settings ----------
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini              # gemini | openai (only needed if both keys are set)
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite  # default; OpenAI default is gpt-4o-mini
# USD_INR=96.28                    # exchange rate used for the Rs cost figures


# -------- What your real .env would look like (made-up values, for shape only) ---------

GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSyXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
SUPABASE_URL=https://abcdefghijkl.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=sb_secret_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ------ Three things to keep in mind  -------------

No spaces around =, and no quotes needed.
SUPABASE_URL is just the base URL. Don't add /rest/v1 at the end.
Older Supabase projects show the service key as a long string starting with eyJ...; newer ones start with sb_secret_. Both work.
